      "title": "plan_api: load and write",
      "action": "Add harness_lib/plan_api.py: load(plan, repo=None) and write(plan, repo=None), both driver entry points that activate the project named by repo (default: the working directory) with load_config(project_root(repo)). load finds the plan by id (padded or not) or path, validates it through plan_doc.load_plan and stores the hash of the file bytes on the plan's private _loaded_hash. write follows the spec's write contract: dump with plan_dict, re-validate the dump, run plan_checks.duplicate_problems, refuse an unknown plan id, a changed base_commit or frozen, a file changed since load, a plan that was not loaded, an extra key at the plan or item level the file does not already carry, and (frozen plan only) any change to an execution field; collect every problem, write nothing on a refusal; render both texts first, then save the JSON, then the PIP; return the re-validated plan.",
